    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d213">

                <pb facs="0265" n="249" sameAs="frus:frus1947v08/pg249"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.79611 PAA/10–1047: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Embassy in Argentina
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-10-10T15:00:00-05:00">October 10, 1947—3
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>960. Panagra has advised Dept they have
                    dispatched air mail letter to their representatives BA authorizing, if not instructing, them to inform Arg Govt, of company’s future operating plans in
                        Arg. Briefly, these plans include
                    inauguration about Nov 1 non-stop services Lima–BA and eventual elimination all Arg
                    stops except BA.</p>
                <p>It is suggested Emb contact local Panagra and discuss advisability (pro and con)
                    divulging such info to Arg until really necessary, or route negotiations settled,
                    whichever sooner. Dept unable cite any specific reasons withhold carrier’s plans
                    at this time but believes question should be weighed by Emb in light possible effect upon current Arg consideration route patterns.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lovett</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
